# Phase 4 — quiet-boot kernel command-line additions for the X16 appliance
#
# cmdline.txt is a SINGLE LINE of space-separated kernel params. Do NOT paste
# these as separate lines — APPEND the tokens below to the end of the existing
# single line in:
#   - DietPi / older images:  /boot/cmdline.txt
#   - Newer Bookworm layout:  /boot/firmware/cmdline.txt
#
# Goal: nothing but the X16 ever appears on screen — no rainbow splash, no kernel
# log spew, no Pi logos, no blinking cursor, no console blanking mid-session.
# Pair with config.txt's disable_splash=1 (rainbow) and DietPi's own boot text.
#
# Tokens to append (all on the one existing line, space-separated):
#
#   quiet                        # suppress most kernel boot messages
#   loglevel=0                   # kernel: emergency-only console log level
#   logo.nologo                  # hide the Raspberry Pi logo(s) at top of screen
#   vt.global_cursor_default=0   # no blinking text cursor on the console
#   consoleblank=0               # never DPMS-blank the console (appliance stays lit)
#   plymouth.enable=0            # no plymouth boot animation (if present)
#
# --- FORCED EDID — the display AND audio fix (see DOC/08-display-fixes.md) -----
# Append this token. It pins the connector to the synthetic 1080p-only EDID, which:
#   * cures "TV won't sync the X16's 640x480 DMT => black screen"
#   * cures the cold-boot connector race
#   * ENABLES HDMI AUDIO — this path runs through the normal connector probe
#     (drm_edid_to_eld), so the audio ELD is populated and vc4-hdmi will open the
#     device. (The runtime debugfs edid_override in custom.sh forces video but
#     does NOT feed the ELD -> ALSA error 524 / no sound. Prefer THIS token.)
# Requires: /lib/firmware/edid/x16-1080p.edid installed (tools/gen_edid.py, which
# now bakes an LPCM audio descriptor into the EDID) AND `dtparam=audio=on` in
# config.txt. Confirm the connector name first with `ls /sys/class/drm/` — usually
# HDMI-A-1 on Pi4 (HDMI-A-2 = second port). Use x16-720p.edid for 720p output.
#
#   drm_kms_helper.edid_firmware=HDMI-A-1:edid/x16-1080p.edid
#
# NOTE: when this token is present, custom.sh auto-skips its debugfs override so
# the two mechanisms don't fight (double-forcing resets the ELD and kills audio).
#
# Example — an existing line like:
#   console=serial0,115200 console=tty1 root=PARTUUID=xxxx rootfstype=ext4 fsck.repair=yes rootwait
# becomes:
#   console=serial0,115200 console=tty1 root=PARTUUID=xxxx rootfstype=ext4 fsck.repair=yes rootwait quiet loglevel=0 logo.nologo vt.global_cursor_default=0 consoleblank=0 plymouth.enable=0
#
# NOTE: keep `console=tty1` — the appliance needs a console tty for KMSDRM to
# become DRM master. Do not remove it while chasing "quiet".
